.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.TOOLCHAIN.LLVM.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.toolchain.llvm.mk
.Nd clang and lld
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read when
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm llvm ,
the default.
It finds clang in the prefixes of
.Xr mk.paths 5 ,
then on
.Ev PATH ,
and sets a matching
.Va CC , CXX , LD , AR , AS
and
.Va RANLIB .
Each may still be overridden.
Clang targets anything, so this is also the file for cross builds, which need
the target's sysroot.
With
.Va ABI Ns = Ns Cm msvc
it hands over to
.Xr mk.toolchain.msvc.mk 5 .
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BMK_MACOS_MIN_VERSION"
.It Ev BMK_LINUX_SYSROOT , BMK_FREEBSD_SYSROOT , BMK_NETBSD_SYSROOT , BMK_MACOS_SYSROOT
The sysroot of a cross build for that system.
.It Ev BMK_MINGW_SYSROOT
A mingw-w64 tree with
.Pa include/
and
.Pa lib/ ,
such as llvm-mingw's.
Otherwise an installed
.Ar triple Ns Pa -gcc
provides them.
.It Ev BMK_MACOS_MIN_VERSION
The oldest macOS to support.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ bmake TARGET=freebsd TARGET_ARCH=arm64 BMK_FREEBSD_SYSROOT=/sr/fbsd
.Dl $ bmake ABI=mingw
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It TOOLCHAIN=llvm: no clang found
Add clang to
.Ev PATH ,
set
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm gcc ,
or set
.Va CC .
.It TARGET=win- Ns Ar arch with TOOLCHAIN=llvm is a mingw-w64 build
The mingw-w64 files or a linker are missing; the message says which and where
they come from.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr clang 1 ,
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.gcc.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.msvc.mk 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
